1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,410
Okay, moving on to testicular tumors.

2
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:04,850
My recommendation before you do this section

3
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:07,010
would be to make sure that you master the section

4
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:09,110
on female ovarian tumors.

5
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:12,230
And that's because once you understand ovarian tumors,

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:14,070
testicular tumors are all downhill.

7
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:16,430
Now, remember that in the female ovary,

8
00:00:16,530 --> 00:00:18,490
we had three compartments that could lead to tumors.

9
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:20,310
We had the surface epithelium,

10
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:22,290
which created surface epithelial tumors.

11
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:24,970
We had the germ cell leading to germ cell tumors.

12
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:26,930
And then we had the sex cord stroma,

13
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,790
which was the connective and supportive tissue

14
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:31,710
of the ovary, which leads to sex cord stromal tumors.

15
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:33,750
Now, fortunately, within the testicle,

16
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:35,210
we don't have surface epithelium,

17
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:36,590
so that makes life a little easy.

18
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:38,750
And so, therefore, there are only two types

19
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:39,830
of testicular tumors.

20
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:41,370
There's the germ cell tumor

21
00:00:41,370 --> 00:00:43,490
and then the sex cord stromal tumor.

22
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:45,550
Patients with testicular tumors,

23
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,510
they present with a firm, painless testicular mass.

24
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:51,110
And, of course, because it is a solid, firm mass,

25
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,890
it cannot be transluminated.

26
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:55,810
Again, this is in contrast to a hydrosoe,

27
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:57,310
which would be transluminated.

28
00:00:57,310 --> 00:00:59,070
Now, one very high yield

29
00:00:59,070 --> 00:01:00,550
and important point to recognize

30
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:03,270
is that testicular tumors are not biopsied.

31
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:06,410
This is against the general principle of medicine

32
00:01:06,410 --> 00:01:08,750
where you always biopsy cancer

33
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:10,070
to prove that it's cancer

34
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,430
and to subtype the cancer.

35
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:13,410
However, in the case of the testicle,

36
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:15,770
this is not performed for two basic reasons.

37
00:01:16,130 --> 00:01:17,870
Number one, if this is the testicle

38
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:18,870
sitting in the scrotum,

39
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:20,450
if a biopsy were performed,

40
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:22,890
you would pull the tumor out from the testicle

41
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:25,370
and potentially seed the scrotum.

42
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:27,170
And, of course, that would not be desirable.

43
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:28,630
So that's the first reason

44
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:30,950
why we don't biopsy testicular tumors.

45
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:34,470
The second reason why we don't biopsy testicular tumors

46
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:36,910
is that the vast majority of testicular tumors

47
00:01:36,910 --> 00:01:38,270
are actually germ cell tumors.

48
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:41,330
In fact, greater than 95% of testicular tumors

49
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:42,390
are germ cell tumors,

50
00:01:42,750 --> 00:01:44,370
and germ cell tumors are all malignant.

51
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:46,370
So, for all practical purposes,

52
00:01:46,790 --> 00:01:49,250
the vast majority of testicular tumors are malignant.

53
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:51,550
Germ cell tumors, as I just mentioned,

54
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:53,270
are the most common type,

55
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:56,070
greater than 95% of testicular tumors.

56
00:01:56,510 --> 00:01:59,490
They usually occur between the ages of 15 to 40.

57
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:02,030
Risk factors include cryptorchidism,

58
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:03,590
or an undescended testicle,

59
00:02:04,010 --> 00:02:05,470
and Klinefelter syndrome.

60
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:08,510
Let's go back and just briefly remind ourselves,

61
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:11,090
as we spoke about when we talked about the female ovary,

62
00:02:11,350 --> 00:02:13,610
that there are really five key germ cell tumors

63
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:15,090
to be familiar with at your level.

64
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,150
Remember that the germ cell has the ability

65
00:02:17,150 --> 00:02:18,390
to make baby tissues,

66
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:21,950
and so therefore you can get tumors of baby-like tissues.

67
00:02:22,290 --> 00:02:23,670
For example, the teratoma,

68
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:25,850
which would represent mature baby tissue,

69
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:27,710
and embryonal carcinoma,

70
00:02:28,070 --> 00:02:30,310
which would represent embryo-like cells.

71
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:31,470
And then, in addition,

72
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:33,690
the germ cells have the ability to make placenta,

73
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:35,790
and when you get a tumor of placental tissue,

74
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:37,490
that's called a choriocarcinoma.

75
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:40,250
The germ cells also have the ability to make yolk sac,

76
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:43,010
and so when you get a tumor of yolk sac,

77
00:02:43,070 --> 00:02:44,210
that's called a yolk sac tumor,

78
00:02:44,210 --> 00:02:46,410
and finally, the germ cells have the ability

79
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:47,890
to make additional germ cells.

80
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:50,470
Now, in the ovary, that was called a dysgerminoma.

81
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:52,250
However, in the testicle,

82
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:53,690
that is called a seminoma,

83
00:02:54,070 --> 00:02:54,850
seminoma,

84
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:56,810
as if it contains sperm,

85
00:02:57,150 --> 00:02:58,690
or germ cell-like cells.

86
00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:01,710
Now, in the case of germ cell tumors within the testicle,

87
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:03,230
remember that all are malignant,

88
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:05,330
and we divide germ cell tumors

89
00:03:05,330 --> 00:03:07,570
into seminoma and non-seminoma,

90
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:09,170
and this is a major division

91
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:10,910
in our understanding of germ cell tumors,

92
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:15,510
and that's because seminoma usually responds to radiotherapy,

93
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:17,750
metastasizes late,

94
00:03:18,050 --> 00:03:20,010
and has an excellent prognosis,

95
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:21,590
versus non-seminoma,

96
00:03:21,690 --> 00:03:23,850
which has a variable response to treatment,

97
00:03:24,350 --> 00:03:26,150
and metastasizes early.

98
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:28,470
So we're going to first start with seminoma.

99
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,870
Seminoma, of course, is a malignant tumor

100
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:34,870
of large cells with clear cytoplasm and central nuclei.

101
00:03:35,270 --> 00:03:37,770
In fact, this description is very similar

102
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:40,470
to the description of dysgerminoma within the ovary,

103
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,670
and so seminoma in the testicle

104
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:45,370
equals dysgerminoma within the ovary.

105
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:47,190
Now, when a seminoma is present,

106
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:49,210
the gross examination of the testicle

107
00:03:49,210 --> 00:03:51,330
will reveal a homogenous mass

108
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:53,070
with no hemorrhage or necrosis.

109
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:55,590
This is how yield examiners like to ask you this,

110
00:03:55,830 --> 00:03:57,970
so that the mass itself will be homogenous

111
00:03:57,970 --> 00:04:00,030
with no hemorrhage and no necrosis,

112
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:02,390
and I'll show you a picture of this in a moment.

113
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:05,550
Rare cases of seminoma can produce beta-HCG.

114
00:04:05,950 --> 00:04:08,830
Now, remember that we classically associate beta-HCG

115
00:04:08,830 --> 00:04:12,230
with choriocarcinoma or the tumor of placental tissue.

116
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:16,550
However, rare cases of seminoma can also produce beta-HCG,

117
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:18,470
and we have already discussed the fact

118
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:20,750
that seminoma has a good prognosis

119
00:04:20,750 --> 00:04:23,050
and responds to radiotherapy.

120
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:24,790
Here's a picture of seminoma.

121
00:04:25,110 --> 00:04:27,570
What we have here are large cells

122
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:30,110
with clear cytoplasm and central nuclei,

123
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:32,590
and, of course, the dysgerminoma in the ovary

124
00:04:32,590 --> 00:04:34,010
would look very similar.

125
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:36,430
Here's the gross picture of a seminoma.

126
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:39,030
In seminoma, recall that it is a homogenous mass

127
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:41,430
with no hemorrhage and no necrosis.

128
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:43,170
And, again, examiners like you to know

129
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:45,170
that it is a homogenous mass

130
00:04:45,170 --> 00:04:47,070
with no hemorrhage and no necrosis.

131
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:50,390
As far as the non-seminominus tumors are concerned,

132
00:04:50,730 --> 00:04:52,950
the first that we'll discuss is embryonal carcinoma.

133
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:55,250
Remember that we're going to divide testicular tumors

134
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:57,030
into seminoma and non-seminoma.

135
00:04:57,350 --> 00:04:59,350
So now we're talking about the non-seminomas.

136
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:01,530
The first would be embryonal carcinoma.

137
00:05:01,850 --> 00:05:03,350
Again, this is a malignant tumor

138
00:05:03,350 --> 00:05:05,090
of immature primitive cells.

139
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:08,590
Again, they're embryo-like, hence the word embryonal.

140
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:11,410
They're very primitive, like the cells of the embryo.

141
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:13,010
It is important to note,

142
00:05:13,130 --> 00:05:15,010
and examiners like to press on this issue,

143
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:18,090
and that is that the tumor can form glands.

144
00:05:18,530 --> 00:05:21,110
It's going to be a hemorrhagic mass with necrosis,

145
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:23,230
and that's because it's a primitive tumor

146
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:24,730
and is rapidly growing.

147
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:25,610
It'll be bloody.

148
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:26,590
It'll be necrotic.

149
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:30,430
This tumor is aggressive with early hematogenous spread.

150
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:32,830
Again, the cells are primitive and embryo-like,

151
00:05:33,130 --> 00:05:34,370
and so they're genetically programmed

152
00:05:34,370 --> 00:05:35,930
to move and spread rapidly.

153
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:38,430
When patients with embryonal carcinoma

154
00:05:38,430 --> 00:05:40,090
are treated with chemotherapy,

155
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,250
an interesting thing that can occur

156
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:43,950
is that the tumor can differentiate.

157
00:05:44,530 --> 00:05:46,950
So because these are very primitive embryo-like cells,

158
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:49,570
that tumor can actually become something more mature.

159
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:52,850
For example, chemotherapy can cause the embryonal carcinoma

160
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:54,110
to become a teratoma,

161
00:05:54,350 --> 00:05:55,830
and that's particularly high yield

162
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:57,310
for board examinations as well.

163
00:05:57,830 --> 00:05:59,550
Now, embryonal carcinoma is very primitive,

164
00:05:59,550 --> 00:06:01,250
and it also has the ability

165
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:04,370
to secrete alpha-fetoprotein or beta-HCG,

166
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:06,150
and that, again, is important to note.

167
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:09,870
Classically, you would associate AFP with the Oaksac tumor,

168
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:12,470
and classically, you would associate beta-HCG

169
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:15,290
with choriocarcinoma, the tumor of placental tissue.

170
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,390
However, it's important to note

171
00:06:17,390 --> 00:06:22,490
that embryonal carcinoma can secrete either AFP or beta-HCG.

172
00:06:23,290 --> 00:06:25,030
Here's a picture of embryonal carcinoma.

173
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:26,670
You've got primitive cells,

174
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:28,770
and in this particular case, they're forming glands,

175
00:06:29,450 --> 00:06:30,990
and I thought this was a perfect picture

176
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:32,850
because, again, examiners like you to know

177
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:36,290
that embryonal carcinoma does have the ability to form glands.

178
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:37,670
Here's a gross picture.

179
00:06:38,030 --> 00:06:40,090
This is the tumor here in the testicle.

180
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:41,950
Again, this is the normal up here,

181
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:45,690
and you can clearly see that this is a hemorrhagic or bloody mass,

182
00:06:46,150 --> 00:06:47,310
and, again, that's indicative

183
00:06:47,310 --> 00:06:51,030
that you're dealing with a non-seminominus germ cell tumor,

184
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:53,670
and, in this particular case, embryonal carcinoma.

185
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:57,550
Oaksac tumor is a malignant tumor that resembles a yolk sac.

186
00:06:57,990 --> 00:07:00,530
It's the most common testicular tumor in children.

187
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:01,450
That's how it yield.

188
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:02,810
So, for your purposes,

189
00:07:02,990 --> 00:07:05,250
when you have a testicular tumor in a child,

190
00:07:05,350 --> 00:07:06,610
for example, a five-year-old,

191
00:07:06,890 --> 00:07:08,610
then you really want to consider yolk sac

192
00:07:08,610 --> 00:07:09,830
on the top of your differential.

193
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:12,290
Now, of course, yolk sac tumor has the ability

194
00:07:12,290 --> 00:07:13,950
to produce alpha-fetoprotein,

195
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:18,490
and so AFP is characteristically elevated in yolk sac tumors.

196
00:07:18,490 --> 00:07:21,430
The characteristic histology of yolk sac tumor

197
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:23,290
is called a Schiller-Duvall body.

198
00:07:23,690 --> 00:07:25,630
Now, this isn't the most common histology,

199
00:07:26,030 --> 00:07:28,110
but it's the classic characteristic histology,

200
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:30,230
and, hence, it shows up on examinations.

201
00:07:30,730 --> 00:07:34,030
This is also called a glomeruloid-like structure.

202
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:37,290
That's the way the examiners like to describe it.

203
00:07:37,370 --> 00:07:39,670
Again, a glomeruloid-like structure.

204
00:07:40,050 --> 00:07:43,110
And the idea here is that this sort of mimics the glomerulus.

205
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:45,370
Let's pretend that this is Bowman's capsule,

206
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:47,310
and this is Bowman's space,

207
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:49,510
and then this is the glomerulus

208
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,170
with a blood vessel running through it.

209
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:53,590
Again, it doesn't exactly look like the glomerulus,

210
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:55,110
but it's glomerulus-like,

211
00:07:55,550 --> 00:07:58,510
and so, therefore, it's called a glomeruloid structure.

212
00:07:58,650 --> 00:08:00,410
And, again, those are called Schiller-Duvall bodies,

213
00:08:00,670 --> 00:08:02,650
and they're characteristic for yolk sac tumor.

214
00:08:03,670 --> 00:08:06,130
Choriocarcinoma is a malignant tumor of placental-like tissue,

215
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:07,610
and so it contains the cells

216
00:08:07,610 --> 00:08:09,450
that normally line the placental villi,

217
00:08:09,710 --> 00:08:12,310
and those are syncytiotrophoblasts and cytotrophoblasts.

218
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:15,310
Now, remember that the syncytiotrophoblasts

219
00:08:15,310 --> 00:08:17,410
are gonna make beta-HCG.

220
00:08:17,590 --> 00:08:19,530
It's high yield to know that the beta-HCG

221
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:21,910
comes from the syncytiotrophoblast.

222
00:08:22,350 --> 00:08:24,430
Now, when the beta-HCG is made by this tumor,

223
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:27,410
that's gonna result in elevation of the beta-HCG.

224
00:08:27,730 --> 00:08:29,630
However, another important thing to remember

225
00:08:29,630 --> 00:08:31,910
is that when you have a high beta-HCG,

226
00:08:32,390 --> 00:08:34,130
the alpha subunit of HCG

227
00:08:34,130 --> 00:08:39,030
is similar to the alpha subunits of FSH, LH, and TSH,

228
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:42,610
and therefore, patients can present with hyperthyroidism

229
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:46,190
because the HCG can activate the TSH receptor

230
00:08:46,190 --> 00:08:49,630
or gynecomastia because the HCG can activate

231
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:51,590
the FSH and LH receptors,

232
00:08:51,810 --> 00:08:54,830
and that's very high yield for the purposes of examinations.

233
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:57,730
Now, this tumor is going to produce

234
00:08:57,730 --> 00:08:59,630
syncytiotrophoblasts and cytotrophoblasts,

235
00:09:00,370 --> 00:09:01,790
so it mimics placental tissue.

236
00:09:02,130 --> 00:09:04,190
However, remember that the functional unit

237
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:05,770
of the placenta was the villus,

238
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:07,250
so that when you look at a placenta,

239
00:09:07,370 --> 00:09:09,770
you've got a villus with a blood vessel

240
00:09:09,770 --> 00:09:10,690
running through the center,

241
00:09:11,010 --> 00:09:13,050
and then you've got the syncytiotrophoblasts

242
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:15,450
and cytotrophoblasts growing around the edge.

243
00:09:16,170 --> 00:09:17,770
However, in the case of choriocarcinoma,

244
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:20,770
it's very important to note that you don't get villi.

245
00:09:20,990 --> 00:09:22,770
You only get the syncytiotrophoblasts

246
00:09:23,610 --> 00:09:24,890
and the cytotrophoblasts.

247
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:27,630
Now, of course, syncytiotrophoblasts

248
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:29,850
and cytotrophoblasts are genetically programmed

249
00:09:29,850 --> 00:09:31,290
to find blood vessels.

250
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:33,690
That's what the placenta does

251
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:35,450
when it implants into the uterine wall.

252
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:38,050
And so this tumor will metastasize

253
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:39,630
very early via the blood.

254
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:41,790
In fact, one of the characteristics of this tumor

255
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:44,530
is that you tend to have a tiny primary

256
00:09:44,530 --> 00:09:45,590
within the testicle

257
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:47,450
and then massive tumor

258
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:48,690
throughout the rest of the body.

259
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:51,290
And that's a little bit against the convention

260
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:53,170
when we think about cancer.

261
00:09:53,490 --> 00:09:54,990
Remember, if the patient's got, for example,

262
00:09:55,070 --> 00:09:56,110
a large breast mass

263
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:57,790
and a tiny mass in the liver,

264
00:09:57,970 --> 00:10:00,350
then we would assume that the breast mass is the primary

265
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:02,250
and that the tiny mass in the liver

266
00:10:02,250 --> 00:10:04,390
is probably metastatic from the breast.

267
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:06,590
However, in this particular case,

268
00:10:06,670 --> 00:10:08,250
you have a tiny mass in the testicle

269
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:10,590
and massive disease throughout the rest of the body.

270
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:12,710
But because you know that choriocarcinoma

271
00:10:12,710 --> 00:10:14,190
rapidly goes into the blood,

272
00:10:14,470 --> 00:10:15,970
you can assume that the primary

273
00:10:15,970 --> 00:10:17,350
is actually in the testicle.

274
00:10:17,730 --> 00:10:19,870
So again, that's important to note as well.

275
00:10:20,710 --> 00:10:22,330
Here's a picture of choriocarcinoma.

276
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:24,250
These are the cytotrophoblasts

277
00:10:24,970 --> 00:10:27,350
and these larger cells, multinucleated,

278
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:29,330
are the syncytiotrophoblasts.

279
00:10:29,330 --> 00:10:31,150
And again, there would be no villi

280
00:10:31,150 --> 00:10:32,930
produced by this particular tumor.

281
00:10:33,830 --> 00:10:35,890
Teratoma is the final germ cell tumor.

282
00:10:36,230 --> 00:10:38,250
This is a tumor of mature fetal tissue.

283
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:41,390
It's derived from two or three embryonic layers.

284
00:10:41,870 --> 00:10:43,590
Now, very high yield to note,

285
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:46,430
teratoma was benign in females.

286
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:49,030
However, in males, it is malignant.

287
00:10:49,710 --> 00:10:51,990
All right, teratoma is benign in females.

288
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:53,990
However, in males, it is malignant.

289
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:58,150
And teratoma can also produce AFP or beta-8CG.

290
00:10:58,590 --> 00:11:00,650
So these are a few high yields

291
00:11:00,650 --> 00:11:02,410
to be aware of concerning teratoma.

292
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,430
Now, although we spend so much time

293
00:11:04,430 --> 00:11:05,690
dividing germ cell tumors

294
00:11:05,690 --> 00:11:07,590
into these very distinct categories,

295
00:11:07,970 --> 00:11:09,870
the vast majority of germ cell tumors

296
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:10,890
are usually mixed.

297
00:11:11,290 --> 00:11:13,690
So, for example, a patient can have

298
00:11:13,690 --> 00:11:15,990
a yolk sac tumor plus a choriocarcinoma

299
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:19,610
or a teratoma plus a seminoma.

300
00:11:20,070 --> 00:11:21,550
And so it's important to remember

301
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:24,390
that most germ cell tumors in the testicle

302
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:25,290
are actually mixed.

303
00:11:25,690 --> 00:11:28,230
And the prognosis is based on the worst component.

304
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:30,790
So, for example, if you have a seminoma

305
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:32,570
and associated with that seminoma

306
00:11:32,570 --> 00:11:33,710
is a choriocarcinoma,

307
00:11:33,970 --> 00:11:35,430
then the prognosis would be based

308
00:11:35,430 --> 00:11:36,670
on the choriocarcinoma.

309
00:11:38,230 --> 00:11:39,310
Sex-cord stromal tumors

310
00:11:39,310 --> 00:11:41,030
are the second category of tumor

311
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:42,610
that can arise within the testicle.

312
00:11:42,990 --> 00:11:44,130
These tumors resemble

313
00:11:44,130 --> 00:11:46,530
the normal sex-cord stromal tissues

314
00:11:46,530 --> 00:11:48,850
of the testicle and are usually benign.

315
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:51,150
Here's an image of the normal testicle

316
00:11:51,150 --> 00:11:53,490
just to remind you of the sex-cord stromal tissues.

317
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:56,610
So the sex-cord includes the Sertoli cells.

318
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,430
And remember that the Sertoli cells

319
00:11:58,430 --> 00:12:00,370
are the cells that line the tubules.

320
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:03,150
And, of course, this area here is the tubule.

321
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:05,610
So you could potentially get a Sertoli cell tumor.

322
00:12:06,010 --> 00:12:08,030
At the same time, you've got these pink cells

323
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:09,630
in between the tubules,

324
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:10,950
which are called lydic cells.

325
00:12:11,350 --> 00:12:13,610
And so you can also develop a lydic cell tumor.

326
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:16,570
Now, lydic cell tumors usually produce androgen.

327
00:12:17,010 --> 00:12:18,530
And so because they produce androgen,

328
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:20,590
you're going to get precocious puberty in children,

329
00:12:21,070 --> 00:12:24,490
or it could also result in gynecomastia in adults.

330
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:27,590
One of the characteristics on histology

331
00:12:27,590 --> 00:12:28,590
of a lydic cell tumor

332
00:12:28,590 --> 00:12:31,030
is that you see these crystals within the cells.

333
00:12:31,350 --> 00:12:32,890
And these are called rinky crystals.

334
00:12:33,070 --> 00:12:34,430
And that's, again, how you'll to know

335
00:12:34,430 --> 00:12:37,230
that lydic cell tumors often have rinky crystals.

336
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:40,030
Sertoli cell tumors will be composed of tubules.

337
00:12:40,110 --> 00:12:41,430
And, of course, the Sertoli cells

338
00:12:41,430 --> 00:12:43,210
are the cells that normally line the tubules.

339
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,950
So the tumor of Sertoli cells

340
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:46,150
will also form tubules.

341
00:12:46,570 --> 00:12:48,810
And these are usually clinically silent.

342
00:12:49,390 --> 00:12:51,030
The final point to make in this section

343
00:12:51,030 --> 00:12:53,450
is that when you have a testicular mass

344
00:12:53,450 --> 00:12:55,210
in the testicle,

345
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:57,130
it's, of course, usually a germ cell tumor.

346
00:12:57,470 --> 00:12:59,730
But that germ cell tumors normally occur

347
00:12:59,730 --> 00:13:01,250
between the age of 15 to 40.

348
00:13:01,630 --> 00:13:04,730
If you have a testicular tumor in a male

349
00:13:04,730 --> 00:13:06,730
greater than the age of 60, for example,

350
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:09,650
then the most common cause would be lymphoma.

351
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:12,490
Again, it's important to note the age of the patient.

352
00:13:12,490 --> 00:13:14,870
Between 15 to 40, you think about germ cell tumors.

353
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:16,350
But greater than the age of 60,

354
00:13:16,490 --> 00:13:19,050
the more common cause of a testicular mass is lymphoma.

355
00:13:19,390 --> 00:13:20,590
This is usually bilateral.

356
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,870
And the lymphoma that develops in the testicle

357
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:26,150
is usually a diffuse large B cell type of lymphoma.

358
00:13:26,590 --> 00:13:28,790
And that concludes our section on testicular tumors.

